{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOjBa2eR9ecAHIZriPBm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to build a workout app UI in Figma across 4 screens (01_Onboarding, 02_Home, 03_Warm_Up, 04_Activity), each 414x896, reusing existing components and media.\n\nI check what I need first. Components 1:23, 1:26, 1:33, 1:44 and the media components sit on other pages of the same file, so instancing them works. Photo instances with image fills copy fine as instances. I load Inter Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold, Extra Bold. The Home Indicator is a 414x34 full-width component sitting at the bottom of the 896 frame. The text field default is 374x75 with a 374x50 input. Page 5:2 is empty, width 0, no children, so I can place frames freely.\n\nI lay out the design system: brand #24C8FE, ink #1B2430 and #0F1B2D, neutral #7A8899, surface #F6F8FB, white. I set category tints (warm-up #FFEDE3, yoga #EAF7F0, squats #EAF2FF, lunge #F3ECFF) and activity colors: running #F77D39, swimming #2BB3E8, cycling #6C5CE7.\n\nType scale: H1 30/36 Bold, H2 24/30 Bold, H3 18/24 Semi Bold, body 15/22 Regular, label 13/18 Medium, caption 12/16 Medium, overline 11/14 Semi Bold.\n\nFor cropping, I place each photo instance inside a frame with clipsContent, scaled to fill or bottom-aligned; the transparent cut-outs work on tinted panels. I build components (SectionHeader, CategoryCard, ClassCard, TodayActivityCard, TabBar, Header, ExerciseRow, DayPill, ActivityCard, Tag) on the workspace page, then instance them into the 4 screens. I start with a read-only check of fonts and the empty workspace, and screenshots of the Media and Components pages.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":11584,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":24074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"e