{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgdupLuLchiNtDLaVDFFV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to lay out a mobile design system and build it screen by screen, and the request is safe to help with as a design and implementation task.\n\nI set the canvas to 414x896, an iPhone 11 Pro Max frame, and fix the tokens first. The brand color is #24C8FE, with ink-900 #0F1B2A, ink-700 #2A3644, muted #7C8A99, subtle #A7B3C0, border #E8EDF3, surface #F5F8FB, and white #FFFFFF. Category tints are Warm up #FFF0E7, Yoga #E9F8F0, Squats #EAF3FF, and Lunge #F4EEFF. Activity accents are running #F77D39, swimming #2BB3E8, and cycling #6B5CE7, with the heart icon at #0074B9 and the selected day in brand.\n\nThe type scale uses Inter: Display 30/36 Bold, H1 26/32 Bold, H2 20/26 Bold, H3 17/22 Semi Bold, Body 15/22 Regular, Body medium 15/22 Medium, Label 13/18 Medium, Caption 12/16 Medium, Micro 11/14 Semi Bold.\n\nFor 01_Onboarding at 414x896 I place a dark status bar on a light background, a centered illustration, the headline \"Best workouts for you\" in Inter Bold 32/38, sub copy \"You will have everything you need to reach your personal fitness goals — for free!\" at 15/23 in muted, and a full-width \"Get started\" button at 374x56 in brand with radius 28, above the home indicator. No tab bar here.\n\nFor 02_Home I stack the elements and add up heights. Status bar 44. Greeting row with a 44 avatar and \"Hello, Adam Smith\" at 17 Semi Bold plus a menu icon, y 44 to 108. Title \"Find Your Workout Class\" at 26 Bold, y 116 to 152. Search field 374 wide, y 156 to 231. Today's activity card, white with a 96 illustration, \"Today's activity\" label and \"8.00 AM - 1.30 PM\", y 247 to 335. Categories header with \"See all\" at 28 tall, y 347 to 375. Four category cards at 108x136, y 383 to 515. Recommendation Class header with \"See all\", y 531 to 559. Class card with photo on top at 366 wide, y 567 to 743. Tab bar 80 tall with the indicator, y 812 to 892. The sum comes to about 743 of content plus the bar, and the remaining gap of 69 keeps it airy; Home may scroll vertically so the frame stays 414x896.\n\nFor 03_Warm_Up I use a back circle with Icon_Back, \"Warm up\" centered, and a more icon. The video cover uses Photo_Seated_Hug on a gradient card with a play button, then the H1 \"Warm up\" and the description, tags for 37.10 mins and Running, an \"Exercises\" header, and 10 exercise rows at roughly 60 to 72 each with a 56 thumbnail, name, duration and play button. The content above the list totals about 426, leaving 392 before the 78 tab bar, so about 6 rows show and the list continues under a sticky bar; I build the scroll content taller and clip it to the viewport so all 10 rows exist as nodes.\n\nFor 04_Activity I place back, \"Your activities\" and more, then \"This week\" with \"Sat 26 – Fri 01\", a seven-day pill row from Sat 26 to Fri 01 with Mon 28 selected, the big 1680 kcal figure, an hourly area chart with 8AM, 10AM, 12PM, 2PM and 4PM and a \"4PM · 120 cal\" tooltip, and Running, Swimming and Cycling cards with time range, hours and km, then the Activity tab current.\n\nI make components reusable: CategoryCard with 4 variants, ClassCard, TodayActivityCard, ExerciseRow, Tag, DayPill (Default/Selected), ActivityCard (3 variants), Button (Primary/Secondary/Disabled/Pressed), TabBar and Header variants. For the 10 thumbnails the reliable route is an image-filled rectangle inside the row instance, overriding fills per row, while the prominent imagery uses real","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42252,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":42252,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id"